replication.must_come_from_the_dump:
Nothing has to come from the dump if live Wikipedia stays reachable. The Batman corpus was itself fetched live, by `study/fetch_corpus.py`, so a live fetch is the like-for-like method.

If a dated snapshot is preferred, the dump would have to supply:

- the 61 source plots;
- the 13 Sherlock episodes and the game;
- the Hound films of 1929, 1937 and 1978, and A Study in Scarlet (1933);
- longer texts for Dressed to Kill (1946) and The Seven-Per-Cent Solution film;
- about a dozen of the non-adapting works.

All my lengths are from the live articles of 8 November 2026. I did not open the November 2023 dump, so I cannot say its plot sections are the same length. The 2017 table shows they can differ a lot: A Study in Terror has 5 sentences there and 25 live.
